# NOTES (history, not open findings)
# - loso_task1.3.py / _output.txt: Task 1.3 two-fold LOSO (RE1-OB <-> RE2-TT,
#   RE1-SS excluded per Task 1.3a). Both folds land at or below their own
#   majority-class baseline (Fold A 0.1760 < 0.2000; Fold B 0.1667 == baseline,
#   total collapse to one predicted class). The script's own scaler-
#   distribution sanity check attributes this substantially to a scaling
#   artifact, not a clean transfer-failure result: kpi_co_breaching_services
#   (a raw, unnormalized count) is near-constant within each system but at a
#   very different magnitude between systems (OB's raw mean lands at -334.8
#   TT-fit standard deviations); kpi_slope_60s and ev_item_count show the same
#   pattern at smaller magnitude; 43/46 features are unremarkable. Treat the
#   headline LOSO numbers as provisional until these raw-count features are
#   dropped or log/ratio-normalized and the fold is re-run -- SUPERSEDED by
#   loso_task1.3_normalized.py below; kept as the pre-fix record, not deleted.
# - loso_task1.3_normalized.py / _output.txt: corrected re-run of the above
#   with kpi_co_breaching_services -> ratio (co-breaching / total distinct
#   services in that case, since RE1-OB has 0 topology nodes so topology size
#   can't be the denominator), kpi_slope_60s -> signed-log, ev_item_count ->
#   log1p. Constant-classifier collapse resolves in both folds: Fold A acc
#   0.1760->0.3360 (macro_f1 0.0607->0.2250, now above its 0.2000 baseline,
#   was below); Fold B acc 0.1667->0.2667 (macro_f1 0.0476->0.2553, now above
#   its 0.1667 baseline, was an exact-baseline single-class collapse). Post-
#   fix scaler check confirms mechanism: all 3 features now sit within ~1
#   TT-fit-std of center (was -334.8, +60.8, -9.92). Residual: kpi_co_
#   breaching_ratio is a constant 1.0 for every RE2-TT case (the underlying
#   "breach" test is weak enough that co-breaching count equals total-
#   services-in-case almost always) -- scale mismatch fixed, but this one
#   feature's within-TT informativeness stays low. Both this and the pre-fix
#   entry above are kept in the trail per instruction; do not delete either.
# - nested_cv_threshold.py / _output.txt: the original run (session 73cfbaa5,
#   script now lost from /private/tmp but its execution independently
#   verified via the Claude Code session transcript at
